course: dictionary
lesson: 1726
title: Words for fruit and flavour
level: primary-5
stars: 2
explain: Context means the words around a word, and they often give clues to its meaning. «Writings from China about 1,700 years ago describe farmers putting weaver ant nests in citrus trees to eat pests.» Farmers put ants in trees, and the ants eat pests, so citrus trees must be trees that grow on farms and bear fruit.
explain: The meaning is a group of fruit trees, and their juicy fruits with thick peel, such as oranges, lemons, limes and grapefruit. Ask: what word would fit here? Then swap in your meaning, «farmers put ants in fruit trees», and check that it still makes sense.
explain: Citrus can also be an adjective, a word that describes a noun. In cooking, a «citrus flavour» is sharp and fresh, the taste of a lemon or lime. The word has two jobs, so check which one it is doing in your sentence.
fact: Citrus means a group of fruit trees, and their juicy fruits with thick peel.
fact: Oranges, lemons, limes and grapefruit are all citrus fruits.
fact: Citrus can be a noun, as in «citrus trees», or an adjective, as in «citrus flavour».
fact: Citrus fruits are full of vitamin C.
fact: Sailors once ate limes to prevent scurvy, a sickness caused by lack of vitamin C.
exercise: «Farmers put weaver ant nests in citrus trees.» What are citrus trees? | Ant homes made of leaves | *Fruit trees with juicy fruit and thick peel | Tall trees that never bear any fruit | Trees with thick bark that grow only in deserts
exercise: Which of these is a citrus fruit? | *Grapefruit | Grape | Cherry | Plum
exercise: Ella says, «The citrus flavour made my tongue tingle.» What does citrus suggest here? | Cold, like ice | *Sharp and fresh, like lemon | Salty, like crisps | Sweet and sticky, like toffee
test: «Sailors once ate limes to prevent scurvy.» What is a lime? | A kind of cheese | A sort of fish | *A citrus fruit, like a small green lemon | A type of ant
test: In «citrus flavour», what does citrus mean? | *Tasting sharp and fresh, like lemon | Tasting of burnt toast | Tasting of salt | Tasting of chocolate
exam: According to «Writings from China about 1,700 years ago», why did farmers put weaver ant nests in citrus trees? | To keep the trees warm | To make the fruit sweeter | To carry seeds to other farms | *To eat pests
